# LLM visibility for public pages

Public HTML pages must be readable by LLMs/agents. Extend the shared registry
and put page Markdown next to the page — do not invent a generic CMS layer.

## Source of truth

1. Add the page to `packages/shared-core/routes/app.ts` (`markdownPages`)
2. Add a page-local Markdown module next to that page
   (e.g. `app/home/homepageMarkdown.ts`, `app/music/musicMarkdown.ts`)
3. Wire it in `app/llm-markdown/pageMarkdown.ts` (`pageMarkdownGenerators` —
   TypeScript requires every registry path)

Path helpers, sitemap, `/llms.txt`, `/llms-full.txt`, Accept negotiation, and
`.md` rewrites derive from the registry. Do **not** edit the proxy matcher for
each new page.

## On the HTML page

```tsx
import { markdownAlternates } from '../layouts/markdownAlternates';

export const metadata = {
  alternates: markdownAlternates(myRoute),
  title: '…',
};
```

Discovery uses `rel="alternate"` metadata, `Link` headers from Accept negotiation,
and `/llms.txt` — not visually hidden DOM hints.

## Do not

- Auth, API, webhook, or OAuth routes — leave them out of `markdownPages`
- Central "generic" Markdown builders for page-specific content
- Hand-maintained `.md` files that can drift from the page
- `ai-content` / `llms` meta tags, User-Agent cloaking, or “for AI only” pages
- Per-page `/api/markdown` handlers — proxy rewrites to `/llm-markdown`

## Verify

- `turbo check:types` (generator map exhaustiveness)
- Unit tests under `app/llm-markdown`, `app/llms.txt`, and `routes/__tests__`
